WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.230 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  the frantic search for 12 young soccer  players and their coach trapped in a  cave complex in Thailand is in its sixth  day the international rescue effort is  focused on caverns in Schenck  rai north of Bangkok a team from the US  military is on the scene the boy's  vanished Saturday when they went  exploring after a soccer game but has  Howard Johnson from our partners at the  BBC reports rescuers have a new reason  for hope  search-and-rescue teams have been  galvanized here today by the improved  weather conditions it's been raining a  lot over the last few days but today the  weather has held what we've seen is a  three pronged approach down behind me  they're been pumping water out of the  cave complex and also a u.s. Navy diving  team has been exploring the caverns and  caves beneath the ground here looking  for the boys trying to find than in this  murky water that has flooded the caves  down there they're part of a 30 strong  US Armed Forces team that I hear and  some of them are also in the hills above  us exploring looking for fissures or  shafts or chimneys to try and rappel  down to try and find the boys that way  now also the type I'm Minister came here  today and took a tour around this camp  he spent more than an hour meeting  search and rescue teams but also spoke  to the relatives of the 13 missing and  he brought a message from the Thai king  and that was that the country would put  all its resources behind finding these  boys Howard Johnson BBC News for CBS  News in Thailand  hopefully the Navy can help bring a  miracle to those boys and their families

